  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Add complete headless and attached configurations for Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex and Cursor.\n- Document installed paths for macOS, Windows and Linux. Distinguish default folders from user-selected folders.\n- Explain asset discovery, supported symbolic links, connection failures and file-path refusals.\n- Link the AI guide to the canonical setup. End both pages with a read-only first check.\n- Keep the existing safety warnings and worked CAM examples.\n\nNo application behavior changes.\n\n## Source checks\n\nChecked against upstream source `9e21ed68247a89819a6cf7c3369a0c29c74f845c`, after v0.26.0:\n\n- CLI MCP argument parsing and the loopback listener.\n- Asset discovery, Windows installer defaults, macOS bundle layout and Linux package layouts.\n- Current primary references: [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp), [Claude Desktop](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/develop/connect-local-servers), [Codex](https://developers.openai.com/codex/mcp) and [Cursor](https://cursor.com/docs/context/mcp).\n\n## Review correction\n\nCommit `76d8575a0ba36ee2503c00c450526d7981ecc673` restores `Codex CLI` in the AI guide for finding 1. No tests changed.\n\n## Checks run\n\n- `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p test_ai_guide.py -v`: all four tests pass on the corrected head. Before the correction: three pass, one fails for the missing `Codex CLI` text.\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD --check`: pass.\n- Existing `xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: exit 0; documentation-only diff selects zero test steps. This is not a Rust test-suite pass.\n- Focused documentation checker: pass. Parse all fenced JSON/TOML, six complete client configurations and Windows path escapes.\n- Execute the two Claude Code command forms against a shell argument recorder: pass. Quoted paths with spaces remain one argument. No real client settings changed.\n- Check internal links and anchors in both guides: pass.\n- Cached `camcraft-cli 0.26.0`: read-only MCP initialization, `tools/list` and `list_operation_types` pass. The tool list has 124 entries.\n- Reproduce the existing AI guide schema-check logic against that cached tool list: all 20 `tools/call` examples pass. The Rust test binary itself was not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo end-to-end sessions in Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex or Cursor. No Windows, macOS, PowerShell or attached GUI execution. Client instructions are source-verified, not client acceptance results. The cached CLI was not rebuilt at the source head.\n\nZola is unavailable; no rendered site build. Internal links and examples were checked directly.\n\nLight lane: Not run. Its release-mode application builds exceed the authorized proportional scope for this documentation-only change. No application, catalog, GUI, workspace or heavy build ran. No paid provider request or machining operation ran.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3029\n",
